 # Existing JSON utility
 
 Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin. Existing action: attempts. Domain functions accept the payload object; api.dispatch routes it. CLI reports ValueError/KeyError with stderr and exit 2.
+
+## Action: schedule
+
+Payload: `{"action": "schedule", "now": <int seconds>, "attempt": <int >= 1>, "base": <positive int>, "cap": <positive int>, "max_attempts": <int >= 1>, "outcome": "success"|"permanent"|"transient", "retry_after": null | <nonnegative int> (optional)}`.
+
+Returns `{"retry": bool, "at": int|null, "delay": int|null}`. Only `transient` outcomes with `attempt < max_attempts` retry. Delay = `max(min(cap, base * 2**(attempt-1)), retry_after or 0)` using exact integer arithmetic; `retry_after` may exceed `cap` and is relative to `now`, so `at = now + delay`. Other outcomes return `false/null/null`. All numeric bounds and `outcome` are validated even when no retry would occur; invalid values raise `ValueError` (CLI: exit 2, message on stderr, no traceback). Input payloads are never mutated.
